Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 13:52:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] docs: link to the getting started guide on
 docs.xen-orchestra.com

User guides now live on docs.xen-orchestra.com; keep the README short
and point to it, to avoid duplicated and diverging instructions.
---
 README.md          | 6 ++++--
 examples/README.md | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 5 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 774542b..b0da34b 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -2,6 +2,8 @@
 
 This builder plugin extends packer.io to support building images for XCP-ng.
 
+📖 **Getting started**: build your first template step by step with the [guide in the Xen Orchestra documentation](https://docs.xen-orchestra.com/automation/packer-provider).
+
 This is a fork of the original builder since the original project was abandoned and no longer compiled with recent versions of Go or worked with Xenserver 7.6 and later.
 
 It improves the original project in the following ways:
@@ -89,8 +91,8 @@ export PACKER_LOG=1
 
 # Documentation
 
-For complete documentation on configuration commands, see [the
-xenserver-iso docs](docs/builders/iso/xenserver-iso.html.markdown)
+- **Getting started**: [Packer plugin guide](https://docs.xen-orchestra.com/automation/packer-provider) in the Xen Orchestra documentation
+- **Reference** of every option: [the xenserver-iso docs](docs/builders/iso/xenserver-iso.html.markdown)
 
 ## Support
 
diff --git a/examples/README.md b/examples/README.md
index 925f61e..2cf866a 100644
--- a/examples/README.md
+++ b/examples/README.md
@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@
 
 In order for new users to get up and running with the packer builder, a few examples of building a machine image with popular distros have been created.
 
-In order to see an exhaustive list of configuration options for the packer builder please see the [following documentation](../docs/builders/xenserver-iso.html.markdown). This doc will focus on the details relevant to the particular distro.
+In order to see an exhaustive list of configuration options for the packer builder please see the [following documentation](../docs/builders/iso/xenserver-iso.html.markdown). This doc will focus on the details relevant to the particular distro.
 
 ### Running the examples
 
